+## Frame rate
+
+**Current: adaptive 60 fps for 2.0.2**, main build `b1f12fd919eae86ab8a978317677e64b`. `fps_target 60` enables it by default; `DM_FPS_TARGET=30` selects 30 fps and `DM_FPS_TARGET=0` runs the original interval selector. Other main builds receive no fixed-address hook.
+
+Trinity's selector at `main+0x1b29660` reads a signed minimum interval from its settings at `+0x20`: 1 means 30 fps, 0 means 60. Simply forcing 0 cannot keep gameplay at normal speed when rendering drops. The hook at `+0x1b296d8` uses the host's adaptive whole-vsync step instead, sets the graphics interval through the original setter (`+0x17fafd4`, object `+0x140`), and rejoins the native paused/unpaused clock dispatch at `+0x1b29738`. Adapters at `+0x1b2a0e4`, `+0x1b5407c` and `+0x29f4214` convert the zero-based interval through the unchanged nanosecond table at `+0x3393e20`. Active clocks therefore receive 16,666,667 ns at 60 fps, 33,333,334 ns at 30, or 50,000,000 ns at 20; paused clocks still receive zero. The host can add a vsync to repay short late frames. Startup uses the selected cap before the first host sample. Long stalls or sustained rendering below 20 fps exceed the shared controller's catch-up limit; this does not guarantee 60 fps on every device.
+
+Original-byte assertions and the main build ID guard every fixed patch site. The frame-step state page is reserved before the appended patch area is aligned; unregistered builds and modules without a frame step keep their original layout.
+
+**Open: frame-time tail.** A historical comparison of main `372a8d8a0404` with candidate `68d75dfab2f9` at target 30 increased frame p99 from 37.6 to 52.3 ms (+39.1%). Both runs had unrelated compiler load, so the increase cannot yet be attributed to load or to the patch. Independent testing at the 30 fps cap is still needed to determine the cause.
+
+Historical station-arrival observations on an M2 Max showed a title screen at 60 fps but station GPU work near 27 ms, usually holding adaptive 30 fps. Native clock measurements tracked real elapsed time during the tested drops. The cap does not guarantee sustained 60 fps.
+
+| Historical station-walk variant | Operation mode | Measured fps | Frame p50 / p99 (ms) | GPU p50 (ms) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Original, target 30 | Handheld | 28.5 | 33.37 / 71.16 | 26.43 |
+| Patched, target 30 | Handheld | 22.4 | 37.05 / 111.35 | 32.77 |
+| Patched, target 60 | Handheld | 20.6 | 49.72 / 77.70 | 36.31 |
+| Patched, target 60 | Docked | 19.7 | 49.34 / 109.89 | 36.35 |
+
+These single samples had changing GPU load; they are not a controlled performance comparison. Runtime coverage is limited to the station arrival, camera movement and short walks with audio disabled. Battles, longer transitions, other cutscenes, full-game progression, audio synchronization, iPhone behavior and sustained 60 fps remain unverified. No controlled runtime stall-injection test or headless validation of display-link/fullscreen pacing is claimed. Detailed environments, commands and results are recorded in the PR.
+
